-- One-time data update: Paris Eiffel Tower Run gets a new layout.
--
-- Its own layout (Moses, 15 Nov 2026: the World Tour re-layouts): until now it
-- was physically the same track as Baqueira-Beret Run and Bobsleigh Run. Down
-- Montmartre past the café tables and street lamps, down the cobbles of the Rue
-- Lepic, a sweep past the Moulin Rouge, right round the Arc de Triomphe on the
-- Étoile (the big feature and new signature: a banked spiral, as the traffic
-- circles it), down the Champs-Élysées, the Concorde hairpin round the obelisk,
-- past the Louvre, down to the Seine, S-bends past Notre-Dame and on to the
-- Eiffel Tower. Its name, slug, look and past races stay. Its track record,
-- country records and players' personal bests start again from now
-- (tracks.records_since); past results stay. Races already run keep their
-- stored replays and play back exactly as they ran.
--
-- Generated from src/game/physicsTracks.js by scripts/physics-track-sql.js --relayout.
-- Only the Paris Eiffel Tower Run track row changes.

